{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And it says <b>and you shall eat and be satiated and bless</b>, for you shall remember the bondage of Egypt and the affliction of the wilderness, and when you eat and are satiated in the good land you shall bless HaShem for it. And our Sages (Berakhot 48a) received that this is a positive commandment, its reason being 'and you shall bless YHWH your Elohim.' And similarly 'and you shall make a parapet for your roof' (Deuteronomy 22:8), and similarly 'and you shall keep the Passover to YHWH your Elohim' (Deuteronomy 16:1), and 'you shall take from the first of every fruit of the ground' (Deuteronomy 26:2), and many others like these. And the meaning of 'for the good land' is like 'and for the good land' — He commands that you bless Him at every time that you are satiated, for the satiety and for the land that He gave you, which He will cause you to inherit forever, and you shall be satiated from its goodness. And behold, the obligation of this commandment applies in every place."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:54.425877843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}